This release adds an independent patch implementation under app.hiro.tiktoklink.patches.
Its corresponding source, build tooling, actual-APK validation evidence and publication
procedures are included in the sources_and_QA archive and at:
https://github.com/hiro191u3n2/hiro-morphe-patches/tree/tiktok-link-v1.0.0/releases/tiktok-link-direct100

The aggregate preserves all existing entries from Hiro Morphe Patches v1.0.306
except the aggregate manifest and the DEX container encoding needed to add new
loader definitions. Existing class definitions, all JVM loaders, extensions,
resources, licenses and notices are preserved. The exact baseline is:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hiro191u3n2/hiro-morphe-patches/72a7fdd39a0ce9d4f4531c3509e90fab6300fe41/downloads/Hiro_Morphe_Patches_v1.0.306.mpp
SHA-256: 04592a32d4475e7af7df6d115d8f611c7f5dc58006da57d0a73c8ae772fa086c

Corresponding inherited source and its notices remain available in this repository
at source commit e79b4084a2821f80b4fa11c9a112728ad07089f3 and the earlier immutable
release source archives referenced by the preserved baseline notices.
https://github.com/hiro191u3n2/hiro-morphe-patches/tree/e79b4084a2821f80b4fa11c9a112728ad07089f3/releases

Morphe and Android build tools are external build dependencies. They are obtained
from their official release locations, verified by SHA-256, and not shipped in
the source archive. TikTok itself and its APKs are not distributed by this release.
No physical Android device validation is claimed.
